65	//! # Engine-level quirks of the original that are reproduced
66	//!
67	//! * Recursion depth limit: the original matcher is recursive and fails a path when its depth
68	//!   exceeds 2998 frames. Frame costs: capture/modifier group 2, k-th of n alternatives
69	//!   min(k, n-1), lookaround 1 (body frames released afterwards), simple (single char/class)
70	//!   repeat 1, complex quantifier: unbounded loop 1 + 2 per optional iteration, bounded
71	//!   optional level 2 if taken / 1 if not, +1 per iteration when the body has captures,
72	//!   mandatory copies 0 (+1 with captures). So e.g. `"ab".repeat(2000).match(/(?:a|b)*/)[0]`
73	//!   has length 999 and `/(a|b)*c/` on `"ab".repeat(200000)+"c"` matches at 399501.
74	//! * Per-attempt step budget (2,000,000 steps of the emulated matcher): when exceeded the
75	//!   attempt at that start position fails and the search continues at the next position
76	//!   (catastrophic patterns return quickly, e.g. `/(?:a|a)*c|a+b/` on "a".repeat(21)+"b"
77	//!   matches at index 4). The step weights are calibrated against the original's thresholds
78	//!   on ~25 pattern families; a few families differ by one input character. No memoisation.
79	//! * Captures set inside a successful positive lookaround are not restored when the
80	//!   continuation fails and an earlier alternative is taken (`/(?=(a))b|a/` on "a" ->
