83	//!   overflow u64 become 0 and skip the order check (`a{99999999999999999999,1}` = `a{0,1}`;
84	//!   `{n,m}` with m < n after overflow runs n mandatory iterations).
85	//! * Named-group mode in non-u patterns is enabled by a naive `(?<` + not `=`/`!` scan
86	//!   (even inside classes/escapes); capture counting for `\N` is class aware.
87	//! * v-mode: set operations and negation work on raw (unfolded) sets, case closure is applied
88	//!   to the final set (`/[^a]/vi` matches "a"; `[\w--[a-z]]` with `vi` matches "a"); inside
89	//!   classes `\w`/`\W` never include U+017F/U+212A. Any single code point operand (`a`,
90	//!   `[a]`, `\q{a}`, `\p{Zl}`) may be a range endpoint (`[[a]-c]`). Lone surrogates are
91	//!   matched by a class range only if exactly one endpoint is a surrogate. `\0` followed by a
92	//!   digit is accepted inside v-mode classes (`[\01]` = {NUL, 1}); `\"` `\'` are valid
